<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wizard Mark</h1>
<p>Sphere: Protection Sphere
Spell Tier: 3
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 80)
Mana: 80
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast wizard mark &lt;object you carry&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster traces sigils on one of their own things and chants 'Proheba 
ethe nau'; a silver rune glows on it and fades away. From then on, if 
anyone else takes it, from your corpse, by stealing, filching or picking 
your pocket, or wears, wields or holds it, a blue flame burns them and 
the thing falls to the ground. The burn is fierce: tens of hit points, 
more the better your magic and your skill in the spell. Then the rune is 
spent, and must be cast again.
</p><p>The mark guards a thing only while it is yours: drop it or give it away, 
and the rune flickers and vanishes. Dispel magic removes it too, and those 
who can detect magic see the mark when they look at the thing. Gods are 
not burned.
</p><p>It takes a strong casting; a poor one just fails. A thing can carry only 
one mark at a time, and some treasures are already protected by the gods. 
You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
